The upcoming iOS 27 and macOS 27 Golden Gate updates expand drawing tools to more of Apple's built-in apps across the iPhone and Mac.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/iOS-27-Messages-Drawing.jpeg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1052253" /><br/>
In the Messages app on iOS 27, there is a new "Drawing" option in the app drawer, which can be opened by tapping the plus sign in the bottom-left corner.<br/>
<br/>
On older iOS versions, the Messages app once had a very basic drawing tool that was accessible by tapping a button on the keyboard in landscape orientation, but now Apple's complete set of Markup tools are available in the app.<br/>
<br/>
On the Mac, macOS 27 adds the Markup tools to the Notes and Freeform apps.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/macOS-27-Notes-Markup-Drawing.jpeg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1052254" /><br/>
